TEXT -96 -200 Left 3 ;#55 Series LC circuit below, at and above resonance
TEXT -96 -144 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hqhV50852jA
TEXT -96 -104 Left 2 ;The generator drives C1 and L1 in series at 20 kHz, at the 33.9 kHz resonance, and at 50 kHz (one stepped run).
TEXT -96 -72 Left 2 ;At resonance V(L1) and V(C1) are equal and opposite, so the stack voltage CH1 nearly vanishes: a short circuit.
TEXT 480 16 Left 2 ;CH1: voltage across the whole C1 + L1 stack (Alan's channel 1).  CH2: voltage across L1 (channel 2).
TEXT 480 48 Left 2 ;V(C1) = CH1 - CH2, the scope math trace.  V1: 4 V p-p open circuit, Rser = 50 ohm generator output.
TEXT 480 80 Left 2 ;Assumed (not stated in the video): L1 = 220 uH with 1 ohm winding resistance, C1 = 100 nF, so f0 = 33.9 kHz.
TEXT 480 160 Left 2 !.tran 0 300u 200u 50n
TEXT 480 200 Left 2 !.step param f list 20k 33.93k 50k
TEXT 480 240 Left 2 !.meas tran VL_PP PP V(ch2) FROM 200u TO 300u
TEXT 480 280 Left 2 !.meas tran VC_PP PP V(ch1,ch2) FROM 200u TO 300u
TEXT 480 320 Left 2 !.meas tran STACK_PP PP V(ch1) FROM 200u TO 300u
